# Testing

## Pick the cheapest level that can catch the bug

| Level | Tool | Location | Runtime |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Domain | Jest, node env | `packages/core/src/**/*.test.ts` | ~1s |
| Component / store | Jest + RTL, jsdom | `apps/web/src/**/*.test.tsx` | ~2s |
| Server module | Jest, node env (`@jest-environment node` docblock) | `apps/web/src/server/**/*.test.ts` | ~2s |
| Journey | Playwright | `apps/web/e2e/**/*.spec.ts` | ~15s |

A pricing rule tested through the browser is a slow test of the wrong thing.
Test the rule in `@fc/core` and let the journey test assert that the number
reaches the screen.

## Rules

- A bug fix ships with a test that fails before the fix. No exceptions.
- Assert behaviour, not implementation. Query by role and accessible name
  (`getByRole('button', { name: 'Thêm vào giỏ' })`), never by class name, never
  with a snapshot.
- Assert error **codes**, not messages. Messages are copy and will change.
- Never weaken an assertion to go green. If the test and the code disagree, say
  which one you believe is wrong and why.
- No `waitForTimeout` as a synchronisation device. Wait for a URL, a response or
  an element. (`expect.poll` is fine for a value that settles.)
- Tests must not depend on each other's order or leftovers.

## jsdom gotchas, already solved

- `jose` is ESM-only and needs WebCrypto: server tests that touch sessions use
  the `@jest-environment node` docblock. `jose` is in `transpilePackages`, which
  is where `next/jest` derives `transformIgnorePatterns` from.
- `jest.setup.ts` runs in both environments, so every `window` stub is guarded.
- `window.location` is non-configurable in current jsdom. Full-document
  navigation goes through `lib/navigation.ts` so tests mock one module instead.

## Playwright specifics

- Runs against `next start` (a production build), not `next dev` — dev-mode
  timing hides hydration and caching bugs.
- Two projects: `chromium` and `mobile-safari`. A commerce checkout breaks on a
  390px viewport first.
- Required fields have a visually hidden `(bắt buộc)` suffix, so their
  accessible name is `"Địa chỉ (bắt buộc)"`. Use anchored regexes:
  `getByLabel(/^Địa chỉ/)`.
- Every spec signs in as the same demo account and the order store is per-user,
  so a parallel run leaves several orders on the page. Scope assertions to the
  order just placed (see the `placedOrder` helper).
- `page.request` shares the browser's cookies; the bare `request` fixture does
  not. Use the bare fixture to prove an endpoint rejects anonymous callers, and
  `page.request` to call it as the signed-in user.
- Rate limits are env-configurable so the suite does not trip the shipped
  login limit. The limiter itself is unit-tested with its own ceiling.

## Coverage

Enforced in `packages/core` (statements 80, branches 75). Treated as a floor,
not a target — a test that exists only to move the number is worse than no test.
